{"title": "Ratio and Proportion (Level 3)", "duration_min": 20.0, "questions": [{"q_en": "<p>The ratio of the number of workers of company A and B is 5:7 respectively and the ratio of their male workers is 4:5 respectively. If the number of male workers of company A is half of the number of workers of company B, then find the ratio of female workers of company A to that of company B.</p>", "q_hi": "<p>&#2325;&#2306;&#2346;&#2344;&#2368; A &#2324;&#2352; B &#2325;&#2375; &#2325;&#2352;&#2381;&#2350;&#2330;&#2366;&#2352;&#2367;&#2351;&#2379;&#2306; &#2325;&#2368; &#2360;&#2306;&#2326;&#2381;&#2351;&#2366; &#2325;&#2366; &#2309;&#2344;&#2369;&#2346;&#2366;&#2340; &#2325;&#2381;&#2352;&#2350;&#2358;&#2307; 5:7 &#2361;&#2376; &#2324;&#2352; &#2313;&#2344;&#2325;&#2375; &#2346;&#2369;&#2352;&#2369;&#2359; &#2325;&#2352;&#2381;&#2350;&#2330;&#2366;&#2352;&#2367;&#2351;&#2379;&#2306; &#2325;&#2366; &#2309;&#2344;&#2369;&#2346;&#2366;&#2340; &#2325;&#2381;&#2352;&#2350;&#2358;&#2307; 4:5 &#2361;&#2376;&#2404; &#2351;&#2342;&#2367; &#2325;&#2306;&#2346;&#2344;&#2368; A &#2325;&#2375; &#2346;&#2369;&#2352;&#2369;&#2359; &#2325;&#2352;&#2381;&#2350;&#2330;&#2366;&#2352;&#2367;&#2351;&#2379;&#2306; &#2325;&#2368; &#2360;&#2306;&#2326;&#2381;&#2351;&#2366; &#2325;&#2306;&#2346;&#2344;&#2368; B &#2325;&#2375; &#2325;&#2352;&#2381;&#2350;&#2330;&#2366;&#2352;&#2367;&#2351;&#2379;&#2306; &#2325;&#2368; &#2360;&#2306;&#2326;&#2381;&#2351;&#2366; &#2325;&#2368; &#2310;&#2343;&#2368; &#2361;&#2376;, &#2340;&#2379; &#2325;&#2306;&#2346;&#2344;&#2368; A &#2325;&#2368; &#2350;&#2361;&#2367;&#2354;&#2366; &#2325;&#2352;&#2381;&#2350;&#2330;&#2366;&#2352;&#2367;&#2351;&#2379;&#2306; &#2325;&#2366; &#2325;&#2306;&#2346;&#2344;&#2368; B &#2325;&#2368; &#2350;&#2361;&#2367;&#2354;&#2366; &#2325;&#2352;&#2381;&#2350;&#2330;&#2366;&#2352;&#2367;&#2351;&#2379;&#2306; &#2360;&#2375; &#2309;&#2344;&#2369;&#2346;&#2366;&#2340; &#2332;&#2381;&#2334;&#2366;&#2340; &#2325;&#2368;&#2332;&#2367;&#2319;&#2404;</p>", "options_en": ["4:7", "3:2", "6:5", "1:2"], "options_hi": ["4:7", "3:2", "6:5", "1:2"], "answer": 0, "solution_en": "<p>Let the number of workers of company A and B is 5a and 7a respectively and number of male workers is 4b and 5b respectively.</p><p>Now,</p><p>4b = &frac12; * 7a</p><p>b = 7a/8</p><p>Ratio of female workers of company A to that of company B</p><p>= (5a  -  4b):(7a  -  5b)</p><p>= (5a  -  4*7a/8):(7a  -  5*7a/8)</p><p>= (40  -  28):(56  -  35)</p><p>= 12:21</p><p>= 4:7</p>", "solution_hi": "<p>Let the number of workers of company A and B is 5a and 7a respectively and number of male workers is 4b and 5b respectively.</p><p>Now,</p><p>4b = &frac12; * 7a</p><p>b = 7a/8</p><p>Ratio of female workers of company A to that of company B</p><p>= (5a  -  4b):(7a  -  5b)</p><p>= (5a  -  4*7a/8):(7a  -  5*7a/8)</p><p>= (40  -  28):(56  -  35)</p><p>= 12:21</p><p>= 4:7</p>"}, {"q_en": "<p>A man divided &#8377;5000 among P, Q, R and S such that the ratio of share of P to Q is 4:5 and that of Q to R is 2:3. If the share of Q is &#8377;375 more than the share of S, then find the share of R.</p>", "q_hi": "<p>&#2319;&#2325; &#2357;&#2381;&#2351;&#2325;&#2381;&#2340;&#2367; &#2344;&#2375; &#8377;5000 &#2325;&#2379; P, Q, R &#2324;&#2352; S &#2325;&#2375; &#2348;&#2368;&#2330; &#2311;&#2360; &#2346;&#2381;&#2352;&#2325;&#2366;&#2352; &#2357;&#2367;&#2349;&#2366;&#2332;&#2367;&#2340; &#2325;&#2367;&#2351;&#2366; &#2325;&#2367; P &#2324;&#2352; Q &#2325;&#2375; &#2361;&#2367;&#2360;&#2381;&#2360;&#2375; &#2325;&#2366; &#2309;&#2344;&#2369;&#2346;&#2366;&#2340; 4:5 &#2361;&#2376; &#2324;&#2352; Q &#2324;&#2352; R &#2325;&#2375; &#2361;&#2367;&#2360;&#2381;&#2360;&#2375; &#2325;&#2366; &#2309;&#2344;&#2369;&#2346;&#2366;&#2340; 2:3 &#2361;&#2376;&#2404; &#2351;&#2342;&#2367; Q &#2325;&#2366; &#2361;&#2367;&#2360;&#2381;&#2360;&#2366; S &#2325;&#2375; &#2361;&#2367;&#2360;&#2381;&#2360;&#2375; &#2360;&#2375; &#8377;375 &#2309;&#2343;&#2367;&#2325; &#2361;&#2376;, &#2340;&#2379; R &#2325;&#2366; &#2361;&#2367;&#2360;&#2381;&#2360;&#2366; &#2332;&#2381;&#2334;&#2366;&#2340; &#2325;&#2368;&#2332;&#2367;&#2319;&#2404;</p>", "options_en": ["&#8377;1800", "&#8377;1725", "&#8377;1875", "&#8377;1935"], "options_hi": ["&#8377;1800", "&#8377;1725", "&#8377;1875", "&#8377;1935"], "answer": 2, "solution_en": "<p>The ratio of share of P to Q is 4:5 and that of Q to R is 2:3.</p><p>P:Q:R = 2*4 : 2*5 : 5*3 = 8:10:15</p><p>Let the share of P, Q and R are 8a, 10a and 15a respectively.</p><p>Share of S = 5000  -  8a  -  10a  -  15a = 5000  -  33a</p><p>5000  -  33a = 10a  -  375</p><p>43a = 5375</p><p>a = 125</p><p>Hence, share of R = 15*125 = &#8377;1875</p>", "solution_hi": "<p>The ratio of share of P to Q is 4:5 and that of Q to R is 2:3.</p><p>P:Q:R = 2*4 : 2*5 : 5*3 = 8:10:15</p><p>Let the share of P, Q and R are 8a, 10a and 15a respectively.</p><p>Share of S = 5000  -  8a  -  10a  -  15a = 5000  -  33a</p><p>5000  -  33a = 10a  -  375</p><p>43a = 5375</p><p>a = 125</p><p>Hence, share of R = 15*125 = &#8377;1875</p>"}, {"q_en": "<p>When 6 sweets from box A put in box B, then number of sweets in both boxes is equal. If 21 sweets from box B is transferred to box A, then number of sweets in box A becomes thrice the number of sweets in box B. Find the ratio of number of sweets in box A to that of box B.</p>", "q_hi": "<p>&#2332;&#2348; &#2348;&#2377;&#2325;&#2381;&#2360; A &#2360;&#2375; 6 &#2350;&#2367;&#2336;&#2366;&#2311;&#2351;&#2366;&#2305; &#2348;&#2377;&#2325;&#2381;&#2360; B &#2350;&#2375;&#2306; &#2337;&#2366;&#2354;&#2368; &#2332;&#2366;&#2340;&#2368; &#2361;&#2376;&#2306;, &#2340;&#2379; &#2342;&#2379;&#2344;&#2379;&#2306; &#2348;&#2377;&#2325;&#2381;&#2360; &#2350;&#2375;&#2306; &#2350;&#2367;&#2336;&#2366;&#2311;&#2351;&#2379;&#2306; &#2325;&#2368; &#2360;&#2306;&#2326;&#2381;&#2351;&#2366; &#2348;&#2352;&#2366;&#2348;&#2352; &#2361;&#2379; &#2332;&#2366;&#2340;&#2368; &#2361;&#2376;&#2404; &#2351;&#2342;&#2367; &#2348;&#2377;&#2325;&#2381;&#2360; B &#2360;&#2375; 21 &#2350;&#2367;&#2336;&#2366;&#2311;&#2351;&#2366;&#2305; &#2348;&#2377;&#2325;&#2381;&#2360; A &#2350;&#2375;&#2306; &#2337;&#2366;&#2354; &#2342;&#2368; &#2332;&#2366;&#2340;&#2368; &#2361;&#2376;&#2306;, &#2340;&#2379; &#2348;&#2377;&#2325;&#2381;&#2360; A &#2350;&#2375;&#2306; &#2350;&#2367;&#2336;&#2366;&#2311;&#2351;&#2379;&#2306; &#2325;&#2368; &#2360;&#2306;&#2326;&#2381;&#2351;&#2366; &#2348;&#2377;&#2325;&#2381;&#2360; B &#2350;&#2375;&#2306; &#2350;&#2367;&#2336;&#2366;&#2311;&#2351;&#2379;&#2306; &#2325;&#2368; &#2360;&#2306;&#2326;&#2381;&#2351;&#2366; &#2325;&#2368; &#2340;&#2368;&#2344; &#2327;&#2369;&#2344;&#2368; &#2361;&#2379; &#2332;&#2366;&#2340;&#2368; &#2361;&#2376;&#2404; &#2348;&#2377;&#2325;&#2381;&#2360; A &#2350;&#2375;&#2306; &#2350;&#2367;&#2336;&#2366;&#2311;&#2351;&#2379;&#2306; &#2325;&#2368; &#2360;&#2306;&#2326;&#2381;&#2351;&#2366; &#2325;&#2366; &#2348;&#2377;&#2325;&#2381;&#2360; B &#2350;&#2375;&#2306; &#2350;&#2367;&#2336;&#2366;&#2311;&#2351;&#2379;&#2306; &#2325;&#2368; &#2360;&#2306;&#2326;&#2381;&#2351;&#2366; &#2360;&#2375; &#2309;&#2344;&#2369;&#2346;&#2366;&#2340; &#2332;&#2381;&#2334;&#2366;&#2340; &#2325;&#2368;&#2332;&#2367;&#2319;&#2404;</p>", "options_en": ["5:4", "13:11", "8:13", "3:1"], "options_hi": ["5:4", "13:11", "8:13", "3:1"], "answer": 0, "solution_en": "<p>Let the number of sweets in box B = m</p><p>The number of sweets in box A = m + 6 + 6 = m + 12</p><p>(m + 12) + 21 = 3(m  -  21)</p><p>m + 33 = 3m  -  63</p><p>2m = 96</p><p>m = 48</p><p>So, the ratio of number of sweets in box A to that of box B = (48 + 12):48 = 60:48 = 5:4</p>", "solution_hi": "<p>Let the number of sweets in box B = m</p><p>The number of sweets in box A = m + 6 + 6 = m + 12</p><p>(m + 12) + 21 = 3(m  -  21)</p><p>m + 33 = 3m  -  63</p><p>2m = 96</p><p>m = 48</p><p>So, the ratio of number of sweets in box A to that of box B = (48 + 12):48 = 60:48 = 5:4</p>"}, {"q_en": "<p>If l:m:n = 1/3:1/8:1/6, then find l/m : m/n : n/l.</p>", "q_hi": "<p>&#2351;&#2342;&#2367; l:m:n = 1/3:1/8:1/6, &#2340;&#2379; l/m : m/n : n/l &#2332;&#2381;&#2334;&#2366;&#2340; &#2325;&#2368;&#2332;&#2367;&#2319;&#2404;</p>", "options_en": ["9:6:32", "6:16:9", "32:9:6", "8:6:9"], "options_hi": ["9:6:32", "6:16:9", "32:9:6", "8:6:9"], "answer": 2, "solution_en": "<p><img width=181 height=37 src=\"https://u1.oliveboard.in/exams/solution/oliveimg/p25764/image001.png\"></p><p><img width=207 height=37 src=\"https://u1.oliveboard.in/exams/solution/oliveimg/p25764/image002.png\"></p>", "solution_hi": "<p><img width=181 height=37 src=\"https://u1.oliveboard.in/exams/solution/oliveimg/p25764/image001.png\"></p><p><img width=207 height=37 src=\"https://u1.oliveboard.in/exams/solution/oliveimg/p25764/image002.png\"></p>"}, {"q_en": "<p>When k is subtracted from each of 33, 48, 63 and 96, the numbers so obtained in this order, are in proportion. What is the mean proportional between 2k and (3k + 1)?</p>", "q_hi": "<p>&#2332;&#2348; 33, 48, 63 &#2324;&#2352; 96 &#2350;&#2375;&#2306; &#2360;&#2375; &#2346;&#2381;&#2352;&#2340;&#2381;&#2351;&#2375;&#2325; &#2360;&#2375; k &#2328;&#2335;&#2366;&#2351;&#2366; &#2332;&#2366;&#2340;&#2366; &#2361;&#2376;, &#2340;&#2379; &#2311;&#2360; &#2325;&#2381;&#2352;&#2350; &#2350;&#2375;&#2306; &#2346;&#2381;&#2352;&#2366;&#2346;&#2381;&#2340; &#2360;&#2306;&#2326;&#2381;&#2351;&#2366;&#2319;&#2305; &#2360;&#2350;&#2366;&#2344;&#2369;&#2346;&#2366;&#2340; &#2350;&#2375;&#2306; &#2361;&#2379;&#2340;&#2368; &#2361;&#2376;&#2306;&#2404; 2k &#2324;&#2352; (3k + 1) &#2325;&#2375; &#2348;&#2368;&#2330; &#2324;&#2360;&#2340; &#2360;&#2350;&#2366;&#2344;&#2369;&#2346;&#2366;&#2340; &#2325;&#2381;&#2351;&#2366; &#2361;&#2376;?</p>", "options_en": ["10", "16", "8", "20"], "options_hi": ["10", "16", "8", "20"], "answer": 3, "solution_en": "<p>The numbers (33  -  k), (48  -  k), (63  -  k) and (96  -  k) are in proportion.</p><p>(33  -  k)/(48  -  k) = (63  -  k)/(96  -  k)</p><p>By componendo  -  dividendo rule  - </p><p>(33  -  k + 48  -  k)/(33  -  k  -  48 + k) = (63  -  k + 96  -  k)/(63  -  k  -  96 + k)</p><p>(81  -  2k)* 11 = (159  -  2k) * 5</p><p>12k = 96</p><p>k = 8</p><p>Mean proportional = &radic;[2*8*(3*8 + 1)] = 20</p>", "solution_hi": "<p>The numbers (33  -  k), (48  -  k), (63  -  k) and (96  -  k) are in proportion.</p><p>(33  -  k)/(48  -  k) = (63  -  k)/(96  -  k)</p><p>By componendo  -  dividendo rule  - </p><p>(33  -  k + 48  -  k)/(33  -  k  -  48 + k) = (63  -  k + 96  -  k)/(63  -  k  -  96 + k)</p><p>(81  -  2k)* 11 = (159  -  2k) * 5</p><p>12k = 96</p><p>k = 8</p><p>Mean proportional = &radic;[2*8*(3*8 + 1)] = 20</p>"}, {"q_en": "<p>A moving body travels a distance (d), varies directly with the time (t) when it moves. A car travels 72 km in 1.5 hours. Find the equation that relates d and t.</p>", "q_hi": "<p>&#2319;&#2325; &#2327;&#2340;&#2367;&#2358;&#2368;&#2354; &#2346;&#2367;&#2306;&#2337; &#2319;&#2325; &#2342;&#2370;&#2352;&#2368; (d) &#2340;&#2351; &#2325;&#2352;&#2340;&#2366; &#2361;&#2376;, &#2332;&#2379; &#2313;&#2360;&#2325;&#2375; &#2330;&#2354;&#2344;&#2375; &#2325;&#2375; &#2360;&#2350;&#2351; (t) &#2325;&#2375; &#2360;&#2366;&#2341; &#2360;&#2368;&#2343;&#2375; &#2348;&#2342;&#2354;&#2340;&#2368; &#2352;&#2361;&#2340;&#2368; &#2361;&#2376;&#2404; &#2319;&#2325; &#2325;&#2366;&#2352; 1.5 &#2328;&#2306;&#2335;&#2375; &#2350;&#2375;&#2306; 72 &#2325;&#2367;&#2350;&#2368; &#2325;&#2368; &#2351;&#2366;&#2340;&#2381;&#2352;&#2366; &#2325;&#2352;&#2340;&#2368; &#2361;&#2376;&#2404; d &#2324;&#2352; t &#2325;&#2379; &#2332;&#2379;&#2337;&#2364;&#2344;&#2375; &#2357;&#2366;&#2354;&#2366; &#2360;&#2350;&#2368;&#2325;&#2352;&#2339; &#2332;&#2381;&#2334;&#2366;&#2340; &#2325;&#2368;&#2332;&#2367;&#2319;&#2404;</p>", "options_en": ["d = t - 48", "d = t/48", "d = t + 48", "d = 48t"], "options_hi": ["d = t - 48", "d = t/48", "d = t + 48", "d = 48t"], "answer": 3, "solution_en": "<p>Distance = d and time = t</p><p>Speed of car = 72/1.5</p><p>d/t = 48</p><p>d = 48t</p>", "solution_hi": "<p>Distance = d and time = t</p><p>Speed of car = 72/1.5</p><p>d/t = 48</p><p>d = 48t</p>"}, {"q_en": "<p>If m is a positive number and n = 8/m, what is the mean proportional of 2m and n?</p>", "q_hi": "<p>&#2351;&#2342;&#2367; m &#2319;&#2325; &#2343;&#2344;&#2366;&#2340;&#2381;&#2350;&#2325; &#2360;&#2306;&#2326;&#2381;&#2351;&#2366; &#2361;&#2376; &#2324;&#2352; n = 8/m &#2361;&#2376;, &#2340;&#2379; 2m &#2324;&#2352; n &#2325;&#2366; &#2350;&#2366;&#2343;&#2381;&#2351; &#2360;&#2350;&#2366;&#2344;&#2369;&#2346;&#2366;&#2340;&#2367;&#2325; &#2325;&#2381;&#2351;&#2366; &#2361;&#2376;?</p>", "options_en": ["16", "2", "8", "4"], "options_hi": ["16", "2", "8", "4"], "answer": 3, "solution_en": "<p>n = 8/m</p><p>Mean proportional of 2m and n = &radic;(2m*8/m) = 4</p>", "solution_hi": "<p>n = 8/m</p><p>Mean proportional of 2m and n = &radic;(2m*8/m) = 4</p>"}, {"q_en": "<p>Reeta put &#8377;5, &#8377;10 and &#8377;20 coins in her piggy bank in the ratio of 7:3:4 respectively and collected a sum of &#8377;4640. What is the total worth of &#8377;5 coin received by Reeta?</p>", "q_hi": "<p>&#2352;&#2368;&#2340;&#2366; &#2344;&#2375; &#2309;&#2346;&#2344;&#2375; &#2327;&#2369;&#2354;&#2381;&#2354;&#2325; &#2350;&#2375;&#2306; &#2325;&#2381;&#2352;&#2350;&#2358;&#2307; 7:3:4 &#2325;&#2375; &#2309;&#2344;&#2369;&#2346;&#2366;&#2340; &#2350;&#2375;&#2306; &#8377;5, &#8377;10 &#2324;&#2352; &#8377;20 &#2360;&#2367;&#2325;&#2381;&#2325;&#2375; &#2337;&#2366;&#2354;&#2375; &#2324;&#2352; &#8377;4640 &#2325;&#2368; &#2352;&#2366;&#2358;&#2367; &#2319;&#2325;&#2340;&#2381;&#2352; &#2325;&#2368;&#2404; &#2352;&#2368;&#2340;&#2366; &#2325;&#2379; &#2350;&#2367;&#2354;&#2375; &#8377;5 &#2325;&#2375; &#2360;&#2367;&#2325;&#2381;&#2325;&#2375; &#2325;&#2366; &#2325;&#2369;&#2354; &#2350;&#2370;&#2354;&#2381;&#2351; &#2325;&#2381;&#2351;&#2366; &#2361;&#2376;?</p>", "options_en": ["&#8377;1120", "&#8377;875", "&#8377;1260", "&#8377;1050"], "options_hi": ["&#8377;1120", "&#8377;875", "&#8377;1260", "&#8377;1050"], "answer": 0, "solution_en": "<p>Let the number of &#8377;5, &#8377;10 and &#8377;20 coins is 7a, 3a and 4a respectively.</p><p>Total sum = &#8377;4640</p><p>5*7a + 10*3a + 20*4a = 4640</p><p>35a + 30a + 80a = 4640</p><p>145a = 4640</p><p>a = 32</p><p>Total worth of &#8377;5 coin received by Reeta = 5*7*32 = &#8377;1120</p>", "solution_hi": "<p>Let the number of &#8377;5, &#8377;10 and &#8377;20 coins is 7a, 3a and 4a respectively.</p><p>Total sum = &#8377;4640</p><p>5*7a + 10*3a + 20*4a = 4640</p><p>35a + 30a + 80a = 4640</p><p>145a = 4640</p><p>a = 32</p><p>Total worth of &#8377;5 coin received by Reeta = 5*7*32 = &#8377;1120</p>"}, {"q_en": "<p>The cost of a pearl is directly proportional to the square of its weight. The cost of a 25 grams pearl is &#8377;3000. This pearl got broken down into two pieces in the ratio of 3:2. How much loss percent is incurred due to this breakage?</p>", "q_hi": "<p>&#2319;&#2325; &#2350;&#2379;&#2340;&#2368; &#2325;&#2368; &#2325;&#2368;&#2350;&#2340; &#2313;&#2360;&#2325;&#2375; &#2357;&#2332;&#2344; &#2325;&#2375; &#2357;&#2352;&#2381;&#2327; &#2325;&#2375; &#2360;&#2350;&#2366;&#2344;&#2369;&#2346;&#2366;&#2340;&#2368; &#2361;&#2379;&#2340;&#2368; &#2361;&#2376;&#2404; 25 &#2327;&#2381;&#2352;&#2366;&#2350; &#2325;&#2375; &#2350;&#2379;&#2340;&#2368; &#2325;&#2368; &#2325;&#2368;&#2350;&#2340; 3000 &#2337;&#2377;&#2354;&#2352; &#2361;&#2376;&#2404; &#2351;&#2361; &#2350;&#2379;&#2340;&#2368; 3:2 &#2325;&#2375; &#2309;&#2344;&#2369;&#2346;&#2366;&#2340; &#2350;&#2375;&#2306; &#2342;&#2379; &#2335;&#2369;&#2325;&#2337;&#2364;&#2379;&#2306; &#2350;&#2375;&#2306; &#2335;&#2370;&#2335; &#2327;&#2351;&#2366;&#2404; &#2311;&#2360; &#2335;&#2370;&#2335;&#2344;&#2375; &#2325;&#2375; &#2325;&#2366;&#2352;&#2339; &#2325;&#2367;&#2340;&#2344;&#2375; &#2346;&#2381;&#2352;&#2340;&#2367;&#2358;&#2340; &#2325;&#2366; &#2344;&#2369;&#2325;&#2360;&#2366;&#2344; &#2361;&#2369;&#2310;?</p>", "options_en": ["55%", "48%", "51%", "42%"], "options_hi": ["55%", "48%", "51%", "42%"], "answer": 1, "solution_en": "<p>Cost of a pearl &#8733; Square of its weight</p><p>3000 = k*25<sup>2</sup></p><p>k = 24/5</p><p>Now,</p><p>Weight of pieces are 3/5 * 25 = 15 grams and 2/5 * 25= 10 grams</p><p>Total cost = 24/5 * 15 * 15 + 24/5 * 10 * 10 = &#8377;1560</p><p>Loss percentage = [(3000  -  1560)/3000] * 100 = 48%</p>", "solution_hi": "<p>Cost of a pearl &#8733; Square of its weight</p><p>3000 = k*25<sup>2</sup></p><p>k = 24/5</p><p>Now,</p><p>Weight of pieces are 3/5 * 25 = 15 grams and 2/5 * 25= 10 grams</p><p>Total cost = 24/5 * 15 * 15 + 24/5 * 10 * 10 = &#8377;1560</p><p>Loss percentage = [(3000  -  1560)/3000] * 100 = 48%</p>"}, {"q_en": "<p>The ratio of the incomes of Keshav and Ratan in the last year was 8:9. The ratio of their individual incomes in the last year and the present year are 6:7 and 3:4 respectively. If their total income in the present year is &#8377;15.36 lakhs, then what is the sum of the income (in lakhs) of Keshav in the last year and that of Ratan in the present year?</p>", "q_hi": "<p>&#2346;&#2367;&#2331;&#2354;&#2375; &#2357;&#2352;&#2381;&#2359; &#2325;&#2375;&#2358;&#2357; &#2324;&#2352; &#2352;&#2340;&#2344; &#2325;&#2368; &#2310;&#2351; &#2325;&#2366; &#2309;&#2344;&#2369;&#2346;&#2366;&#2340; 8:9 &#2341;&#2366;&#2404; &#2346;&#2367;&#2331;&#2354;&#2375; &#2357;&#2352;&#2381;&#2359; &#2324;&#2352; &#2357;&#2352;&#2381;&#2340;&#2350;&#2366;&#2344; &#2357;&#2352;&#2381;&#2359; &#2350;&#2375;&#2306; &#2313;&#2344;&#2325;&#2368; &#2357;&#2381;&#2351;&#2325;&#2381;&#2340;&#2367;&#2327;&#2340; &#2310;&#2351; &#2325;&#2366; &#2309;&#2344;&#2369;&#2346;&#2366;&#2340; &#2325;&#2381;&#2352;&#2350;&#2358;&#2307; 6:7 &#2324;&#2352; 3:4 &#2361;&#2376;&#2404; &#2351;&#2342;&#2367; &#2357;&#2352;&#2381;&#2340;&#2350;&#2366;&#2344; &#2357;&#2352;&#2381;&#2359; &#2350;&#2375;&#2306; &#2313;&#2344;&#2325;&#2368; &#2325;&#2369;&#2354; &#2310;&#2351; 15.36 &#2354;&#2366;&#2326; &#2352;&#2369;&#2346;&#2351;&#2375; &#2361;&#2376;, &#2340;&#2379; &#2346;&#2367;&#2331;&#2354;&#2375; &#2357;&#2352;&#2381;&#2359; &#2325;&#2375;&#2358;&#2357; &#2325;&#2368; &#2310;&#2351; &#2324;&#2352; &#2357;&#2352;&#2381;&#2340;&#2350;&#2366;&#2344; &#2357;&#2352;&#2381;&#2359; &#2350;&#2375;&#2306; &#2352;&#2340;&#2344; &#2325;&#2368; &#2310;&#2351; &#2325;&#2366; &#2351;&#2379;&#2327; (&#2354;&#2366;&#2326;&#2379;&#2306; &#2350;&#2375;&#2306;) &#2325;&#2381;&#2351;&#2366; &#2361;&#2376;?</p>", "options_en": ["14.4", "18.5", "13.2", "21.25"], "options_hi": ["14.4", "18.5", "13.2", "21.25"], "answer": 0, "solution_en": "<p>Let the income of Keshav and Ratan in the last year was &#8377;8p and &#8377;9p respectively.</p><p>Total income of Keshav in the present year = 8p*7/6 = 28p/3</p><p>Total income of Ratan in the present year = 9p*4/3 = 12p</p><p>Now,</p><p>28p/3 + 12p = 15.36 lakh</p><p>64p/3 = 15.36</p><p>p = 72000</p><p>Sum of the income of Keshav in the last year and that of Ratan in the present year = 8*72000 + 12*72000 = 14.4 lakhs</p>", "solution_hi": "<p>Let the income of Keshav and Ratan in the last year was &#8377;8p and &#8377;9p respectively.</p><p>Total income of Keshav in the present year = 8p*7/6 = 28p/3</p><p>Total income of Ratan in the present year = 9p*4/3 = 12p</p><p>Now,</p><p>28p/3 + 12p = 15.36 lakh</p><p>64p/3 = 15.36</p><p>p = 72000</p><p>Sum of the income of Keshav in the last year and that of Ratan in the present year = 8*72000 + 12*72000 = 14.4 lakhs</p>"}, {"q_en": "<p>A has a sum of &#8377;450 and he wants to pay the sum to B by using coins of &#8377;2, &#8377;5 and &#8377;10. He uses a total of 109 coins. If the ratio of &#8377;2 and &#8377;5 coins used is 5:8, then how many coins of &#8377;10 are used in the payment?</p>", "q_hi": "<p>A &#2325;&#2375; &#2346;&#2366;&#2360; &#8377;450 &#2325;&#2368; &#2352;&#2366;&#2358;&#2367; &#2361;&#2376; &#2324;&#2352; &#2357;&#2361; &#8377;2, &#8377;5 &#2324;&#2352; &#8377;10 &#2325;&#2375; &#2360;&#2367;&#2325;&#2381;&#2325;&#2379;&#2306; &#2325;&#2366; &#2313;&#2346;&#2351;&#2379;&#2327; &#2325;&#2352;&#2325;&#2375; B &#2325;&#2379; &#2351;&#2361; &#2352;&#2366;&#2358;&#2367; &#2342;&#2375;&#2344;&#2366; &#2330;&#2366;&#2361;&#2340;&#2366; &#2361;&#2376;&#2404; &#2357;&#2361; &#2325;&#2369;&#2354; 109 &#2360;&#2367;&#2325;&#2381;&#2325;&#2379;&#2306; &#2325;&#2366; &#2313;&#2346;&#2351;&#2379;&#2327; &#2325;&#2352;&#2340;&#2366; &#2361;&#2376;&#2404; &#2351;&#2342;&#2367; &#2313;&#2346;&#2351;&#2379;&#2327; &#2325;&#2367;&#2319; &#2327;&#2319; &#8377;2 &#2324;&#2352; &#8377;5 &#2325;&#2375; &#2360;&#2367;&#2325;&#2381;&#2325;&#2379;&#2306; &#2325;&#2366; &#2309;&#2344;&#2369;&#2346;&#2366;&#2340; 5:8 &#2361;&#2376;, &#2340;&#2379; &#2349;&#2369;&#2327;&#2340;&#2366;&#2344; &#2350;&#2375;&#2306; &#8377;10 &#2325;&#2375; &#2325;&#2367;&#2340;&#2344;&#2375; &#2360;&#2367;&#2325;&#2381;&#2325;&#2379;&#2306; &#2325;&#2366; &#2313;&#2346;&#2351;&#2379;&#2327; &#2325;&#2367;&#2351;&#2366; &#2327;&#2351;&#2366;?</p>", "options_en": ["6", "2", "5", "8"], "options_hi": ["6", "2", "5", "8"], "answer": 2, "solution_en": "<p>Total number of coins of &#8377;2 and &#8377;5 are 5n and 8n respectively.</p><p>Total number of coins of &#8377;10 = 109  -  5n  -  8n = 109  -  13n</p><p>Now,</p><p>2*5n + 5*8n + 10*(109  -  13n) = 450</p><p>10n + 40n + 1090  -  130n = 450</p><p>80n = 640</p><p>n = 8</p><p>Total number of coins of &#8377;10 are used in the payment = 109  -  13*8 = 5</p>", "solution_hi": "<p>Total number of coins of &#8377;2 and &#8377;5 are 5n and 8n respectively.</p><p>Total number of coins of &#8377;10 = 109  -  5n  -  8n = 109  -  13n</p><p>Now,</p><p>2*5n + 5*8n + 10*(109  -  13n) = 450</p><p>10n + 40n + 1090  -  130n = 450</p><p>80n = 640</p><p>n = 8</p><p>Total number of coins of &#8377;10 are used in the payment = 109  -  13*8 = 5</p>"}, {"q_en": "<p>If x varies directly as square of y and inversely as z and when y = 2 and z = 3, x = 8, find the value of x when y = 6 and z = 18.</p>", "q_hi": "<p>&#2351;&#2342;&#2367; x, y &#2325;&#2375; &#2357;&#2352;&#2381;&#2327; &#2325;&#2375; &#2360;&#2350;&#2366;&#2344;&#2369;&#2346;&#2366;&#2340;&#2368; &#2340;&#2341;&#2366; z &#2325;&#2375; &#2357;&#2381;&#2351;&#2369;&#2340;&#2381;&#2325;&#2381;&#2352;&#2350;&#2366;&#2344;&#2369;&#2346;&#2366;&#2340;&#2368; &#2361;&#2379;&#2340;&#2366; &#2361;&#2376; &#2340;&#2341;&#2366; &#2332;&#2348; y = 2 &#2340;&#2341;&#2366; z = 3, x = 8 &#2361;&#2376;, &#2340;&#2379; x &#2325;&#2366; &#2350;&#2366;&#2344; &#2332;&#2381;&#2334;&#2366;&#2340; &#2325;&#2368;&#2332;&#2367;&#2319; &#2332;&#2348; y = 6 &#2340;&#2341;&#2366; z = 18 &#2361;&#2376;&#2404;</p>", "options_en": ["10", "12", "9", "15"], "options_hi": ["10", "12", "9", "15"], "answer": 1, "solution_en": "<p>x &#8733; y<sup>2</sup>/z</p><p>x = ky<sup>2</sup>/z</p><p>When y = 2 and z = 3 =&gt; x= 8</p><p>8 = k * 2<sup>2</sup>/3</p><p>k = 6</p><p>When y = 6 and z = 18</p><p>x = 6 * 6<sup>2</sup>/18</p><p>x = 12</p>", "solution_hi": "<p>x &#8733; y<sup>2</sup>/z</p><p>x = ky<sup>2</sup>/z</p><p>When y = 2 and z = 3 =&gt; x= 8</p><p>8 = k * 2<sup>2</sup>/3</p><p>k = 6</p><p>When y = 6 and z = 18</p><p>x = 6 * 6<sup>2</sup>/18</p><p>x = 12</p>"}, {"q_en": "<p>What is the compound ratio of the inverse ratios of the ratios ab : cd, ac : bd, bc : ad?</p>", "q_hi": "<p>&#2309;&#2344;&#2369;&#2346;&#2366;&#2340; ab : cd, ac : bd, bc : ad &#2325;&#2375; &#2357;&#2381;&#2351;&#2369;&#2340;&#2381;&#2325;&#2381;&#2352;&#2350; &#2309;&#2344;&#2369;&#2346;&#2366;&#2340;&#2379;&#2306; &#2325;&#2366; &#2350;&#2367;&#2358;&#2381;&#2352;&#2367;&#2340; &#2309;&#2344;&#2369;&#2346;&#2366;&#2340; &#2325;&#2381;&#2351;&#2366; &#2361;&#2376;?</p>", "options_en": ["d<sup>3</sup> : abc", "1 : abcd", "ab : cd", "acd : b<sup>3</sup>"], "options_hi": ["d<sup>3</sup> : abc", "1 : abcd", "ab : cd", "acd : b<sup>3</sup>"], "answer": 0, "solution_en": "<p>Inverse ratios of the ratios ab:cd, ac:bd, bc:ad = cd:ab, bd:ac, ad:bc</p><p>Compound ratio = Product of numerator of ratios : Product of denominator of ratios</p><p>= (cd*bd*ad) : (ab*ac*bc)</p><p>= d<sup>3</sup> : abc</p>", "solution_hi": "<p>Inverse ratios of the ratios ab:cd, ac:bd, bc:ad = cd:ab, bd:ac, ad:bc</p><p>Compound ratio = Product of numerator of ratios : Product of denominator of ratios</p><p>= (cd*bd*ad) : (ab*ac*bc)</p><p>= d<sup>3</sup> : abc</p>"}, {"q_en": "<p>A sum of &#8377;68400 is divided among P, Q, R and S such that the ratio of share of P and Q together to the share of R and S together is 25:13 and the ratio of share of P to Q is 7:8. The share of S is &#8377;8400. If y is the difference between share of P and R and z is the difference between share of Q and S, then find the value of (z  -  2y)?</p>", "q_hi": "<p>&#8377;68400 &#2325;&#2368; &#2352;&#2366;&#2358;&#2367; &#2325;&#2379; P, Q, R &#2324;&#2352; S &#2325;&#2375; &#2348;&#2368;&#2330; &#2311;&#2360; &#2346;&#2381;&#2352;&#2325;&#2366;&#2352; &#2348;&#2366;&#2306;&#2335;&#2366; &#2332;&#2366;&#2340;&#2366; &#2361;&#2376; &#2325;&#2367; P &#2324;&#2352; Q &#2325;&#2375; &#2361;&#2367;&#2360;&#2381;&#2360;&#2375; &#2325;&#2366; R &#2324;&#2352; S &#2325;&#2375; &#2361;&#2367;&#2360;&#2381;&#2360;&#2375; &#2360;&#2375; &#2309;&#2344;&#2369;&#2346;&#2366;&#2340; 25:13 &#2361;&#2376; &#2324;&#2352; P &#2324;&#2352; Q &#2325;&#2375; &#2361;&#2367;&#2360;&#2381;&#2360;&#2375; &#2325;&#2366; &#2309;&#2344;&#2369;&#2346;&#2366;&#2340; 7:8 &#2361;&#2376;&#2404; S &#2325;&#2366; &#2361;&#2367;&#2360;&#2381;&#2360;&#2366; &#8377;8400 &#2361;&#2376;&#2404; &#2351;&#2342;&#2367; y, P &#2324;&#2352; R &#2325;&#2375; &#2361;&#2367;&#2360;&#2381;&#2360;&#2375; &#2325;&#2375; &#2348;&#2368;&#2330; &#2325;&#2366; &#2309;&#2306;&#2340;&#2352; &#2361;&#2376; &#2324;&#2352; z, Q &#2324;&#2352; S &#2325;&#2375; &#2361;&#2367;&#2360;&#2381;&#2360;&#2375; &#2325;&#2375; &#2348;&#2368;&#2330; &#2325;&#2366; &#2309;&#2306;&#2340;&#2352; &#2361;&#2376;, &#2340;&#2379; (z - 2y) &#2325;&#2366; &#2350;&#2366;&#2344; &#2332;&#2381;&#2334;&#2366;&#2340; &#2325;&#2368;&#2332;&#2367;&#2319;?</p>", "options_en": ["&#8377;3600", "&#8377;4200", "&#8377;3000", "&#8377;4800"], "options_hi": ["&#8377;3600", "&#8377;4200", "&#8377;3000", "&#8377;4800"], "answer": 0, "solution_en": "<p>Total amount = &#8377;68400</p><p>P/Q = 7/8 =&gt; P = 7Q/8</p><p>Now,</p><p>(P + Q)/(R + S) = 25/13</p><p>13(P + Q) = 25(R + S)</p><p>13(P + Q) = 25(68400  -  P  -  Q)</p><p>38(P + Q) = 25*68400</p><p>7Q/8 + Q = 45000</p><p>Q = &#8377;24000</p><p>P = 7*24000/8 = &#8377;21000</p><p>S = &#8377;8400</p><p>R = 68400  -  (21000 + 24000 + 8400) = &#8377;15000</p><p>y = difference between share of P and R = 21000  -  15000 = &#8377;6000</p><p>z = difference between share of Q and S = 24000  -  8400 = &#8377;15600</p><p>z  -  2y = 15600  -  2*6000 = &#8377;3600</p>", "solution_hi": "<p>Total amount = &#8377;68400</p><p>P/Q = 7/8 =&gt; P = 7Q/8</p><p>Now,</p><p>(P + Q)/(R + S) = 25/13</p><p>13(P + Q) = 25(R + S)</p><p>13(P + Q) = 25(68400  -  P  -  Q)</p><p>38(P + Q) = 25*68400</p><p>7Q/8 + Q = 45000</p><p>Q = &#8377;24000</p><p>P = 7*24000/8 = &#8377;21000</p><p>S = &#8377;8400</p><p>R = 68400  -  (21000 + 24000 + 8400) = &#8377;15000</p><p>y = difference between share of P and R = 21000  -  15000 = &#8377;6000</p><p>z = difference between share of Q and S = 24000  -  8400 = &#8377;15600</p><p>z  -  2y = 15600  -  2*6000 = &#8377;3600</p>"}, {"q_en": "<p>If p, q and r are positive numbers such that (p<sup>2</sup> + q<sup>2</sup>) : (q<sup>2</sup> + r<sup>2</sup>) : (r<sup>2</sup> + p<sup>2</sup>) = 52:25:45, then pq : qr : rp = _____.</p>", "q_hi": "<p>&#2351;&#2342;&#2367; p, q &#2324;&#2352; r &#2343;&#2344;&#2366;&#2340;&#2381;&#2350;&#2325; &#2360;&#2306;&#2326;&#2381;&#2351;&#2366;&#2319;&#2305; &#2361;&#2376;&#2306; &#2332;&#2376;&#2360;&#2375; &#2325;&#2367; (p<sup>2</sup> + q<sup>2</sup>) : (q<sup>2</sup> + r<sup>2</sup>) : (r<sup>2</sup> + p<sup>2</sup>) = 52:25:45, &#2340;&#2379; pq : qr : rp = _____.</p>", "options_en": ["1:4:2", "4:2:3", "3:2:6", "2:1:3"], "options_hi": ["1:4:2", "4:2:3", "3:2:6", "2:1:3"], "answer": 1, "solution_en": "<p>(p<sup>2</sup> + q<sup>2</sup>) : (q<sup>2</sup> + r<sup>2</sup>) : (r<sup>2</sup> + p<sup>2</sup>) = 52:25:45</p><p>p<sup>2</sup> + q<sup>2</sup> + q<sup>2</sup> + r<sup>2</sup> + r<sup>2</sup> + p<sup>2</sup> = 52 + 25 + 45</p><p>p<sup>2</sup> + q<sup>2</sup> + r<sup>2</sup> = 61</p><p>Now,</p><p>(p<sup>2</sup> + q<sup>2</sup> + r<sup>2</sup>)  -  (q<sup>2</sup> + r<sup>2</sup>) = 61  -  25</p><p>p<sup>2</sup> = 36</p><p>p = 6</p><p>(p<sup>2</sup> + q<sup>2</sup> + r<sup>2</sup>)  -  (r<sup>2</sup> + p<sup>2</sup>) = 61  -  45</p><p>q<sup>2</sup> = 16</p><p>q = 4</p><p>(p<sup>2</sup> + q<sup>2</sup> + r<sup>2</sup>)  -  (p<sup>2</sup> + q<sup>2</sup>) = 61  -  52</p><p>r<sup>2</sup> = 9</p><p>r = 3</p><p>pq : qr : rp = 6*4 : 4*3 : 3*6 = 4:2:3</p>", "solution_hi": "<p>(p<sup>2</sup> + q<sup>2</sup>) : (q<sup>2</sup> + r<sup>2</sup>) : (r<sup>2</sup> + p<sup>2</sup>) = 52:25:45</p><p>p<sup>2</sup> + q<sup>2</sup> + q<sup>2</sup> + r<sup>2</sup> + r<sup>2</sup> + p<sup>2</sup> = 52 + 25 + 45</p><p>p<sup>2</sup> + q<sup>2</sup> + r<sup>2</sup> = 61</p><p>Now,</p><p>(p<sup>2</sup> + q<sup>2</sup> + r<sup>2</sup>)  -  (q<sup>2</sup> + r<sup>2</sup>) = 61  -  25</p><p>p<sup>2</sup> = 36</p><p>p = 6</p><p>(p<sup>2</sup> + q<sup>2</sup> + r<sup>2</sup>)  -  (r<sup>2</sup> + p<sup>2</sup>) = 61  -  45</p><p>q<sup>2</sup> = 16</p><p>q = 4</p><p>(p<sup>2</sup> + q<sup>2</sup> + r<sup>2</sup>)  -  (p<sup>2</sup> + q<sup>2</sup>) = 61  -  52</p><p>r<sup>2</sup> = 9</p><p>r = 3</p><p>pq : qr : rp = 6*4 : 4*3 : 3*6 = 4:2:3</p>"}, {"q_en": "<p>The time 't' to go over a fixed distance is in reverse proportion to the average speed 'v' of the vehicle. When the average speed of the vehicle is 50 km/hr it takes 6 hours to go over a certain distance. Find the time (in hrs) required to cover the same distance at an average speed of 60 km/hr?</p>", "q_hi": "<p>&#2351;&#2342;&#2367; &#2319;&#2325; &#2344;&#2367;&#2358;&#2381;&#2330;&#2367;&#2340; &#2342;&#2370;&#2352;&#2368; &#2340;&#2351; &#2325;&#2352;&#2344;&#2375; &#2350;&#2375;&#2306; &#2354;&#2327;&#2344;&#2375; &#2357;&#2366;&#2354;&#2366; &#2360;&#2350;&#2351; 'T' &#2357;&#2366;&#2361;&#2344; &#2325;&#2368; &#2324;&#2360;&#2340; &#2327;&#2340;&#2367; 'V' &#2325;&#2375; &#2313;&#2354;&#2335;&#2375; &#2360;&#2350;&#2366;&#2344;&#2369;&#2346;&#2366;&#2340; &#2350;&#2375;&#2306; &#2361;&#2376;&#2404; &#2332;&#2348; &#2357;&#2366;&#2361;&#2344; &#2325;&#2368; &#2324;&#2360;&#2340; &#2327;&#2340;&#2367; 50 &#2325;&#2367;&#2350;&#2368;/&#2328;&#2306;&#2335;&#2366; &#2361;&#2376; &#2340;&#2379; &#2319;&#2325; &#2344;&#2367;&#2358;&#2381;&#2330;&#2367;&#2340; &#2342;&#2370;&#2352;&#2368; &#2340;&#2351; &#2325;&#2352;&#2344;&#2375; &#2325;&#2375; &#2354;&#2367;&#2319; 6 &#2328;&#2306;&#2335;&#2375; &#2354;&#2327;&#2340;&#2375; &#2361;&#2376;&#2306;&#2404; 60 &#2325;&#2367;&#2350;&#2368;/&#2328;&#2306;&#2335;&#2366; &#2325;&#2368; &#2324;&#2360;&#2340; &#2327;&#2340;&#2367; &#2360;&#2375; &#2313;&#2360;&#2368; &#2342;&#2370;&#2352;&#2368; &#2325;&#2379; &#2340;&#2351; &#2325;&#2352;&#2344;&#2375; &#2350;&#2375;&#2306; &#2354;&#2327;&#2366; &#2360;&#2350;&#2351; (&#2328;&#2306;&#2335;&#2375; &#2350;&#2375;&#2306;) &#2332;&#2381;&#2334;&#2366;&#2340; &#2325;&#2352;&#2375;&#2306;?</p>", "options_en": ["2.5", "4", "6", "5"], "options_hi": ["2.5", "4", "6", "5"], "answer": 3, "solution_en": "<p>t &prop; 1/v or t = k/v </p><p>6 = k/50 or k = 300</p><p>At 60 km/hr, t = 300/60 = 5</p>", "solution_hi": "<p>t &prop; 1/v or t = k/v </p><p>6 = k/50 or k = 300</p><p>At 60 km/hr, t = 300/60 = 5</p>"}, {"q_en": "<p>If p: q = 6: 5, q: r = 7: 10 (p and r are coprime natural numbers), then what is the value of p<sup>2</sup> + r<sup>2</sup>.</p>", "q_hi": "<p>&#2351;&#2342;&#2367; p: q = 6: 5, q: r = 7: 10 (p &#2324;&#2352; r &#2360;&#2361;&#2309;&#2349;&#2366;&#2332;&#2381;&#2351; &#2346;&#2381;&#2352;&#2366;&#2325;&#2371;&#2340; &#2360;&#2306;&#2326;&#2381;&#2351;&#2366;&#2319;&#2305; &#2361;&#2376;&#2306;), &#2340;&#2379; p<sup>2</sup> + r<sup>2</sup> &#2325;&#2366; &#2350;&#2366;&#2344; &#2325;&#2367;&#2340;&#2344;&#2366; &#2361;&#2376;&#2404;</p>", "options_en": ["1025", "1066", "1177", "1013"], "options_hi": ["1025", "1066", "1177", "1013"], "answer": 1, "solution_en": "<p>p: q = 6: 5</p><p>q: r = 7: 10</p><p>p: q: r = (6 * 7): (5 * 7): (5 * 10) = 42: 35: 50</p><p>p: r = 42: 50 = 21: 25</p><p>Since p and r are coprime natural numbers.</p><p>p = 21 and q = 25</p><p>Now,</p><p>p<sup>2</sup> + r<sup>2</sup></p><p>= 21<sup>2</sup> + 25<sup>2</sup></p><p>= 441 + 625</p><p>= 1066</p>", "solution_hi": "<p>p: q = 6: 5</p><p>q: r = 7: 10</p><p>p: q: r = (6 * 7): (5 * 7): (5 * 10) = 42: 35: 50</p><p>p: r = 42: 50 = 21: 25</p><p>Since p and r are coprime natural numbers.</p><p>p = 21 and q = 25</p><p>Now,</p><p>p<sup>2</sup> + r<sup>2</sup></p><p>= 21<sup>2</sup> + 25<sup>2</sup></p><p>= 441 + 625</p><p>= 1066</p>"}, {"q_en": "<p><div>&nbsp;Respective ratio of incomes of three persons A, B and C in Jan is&nbsp;<div style=\"display: inline-block;position: relative;vertical-align: middle;\"><span style=\"text-align:center;display: block; padding: 0;\">1</span><span style=\"display: block; padding: 0;position: absolute; top: 0em; display: none;letter-spacing: -0.1em;\">_________</span><span style=\"display: block; padding: 0;border-top: thin solid black; text-align:center\">30</span></div>&nbsp;:&nbsp;<div style=\"display: inline-block;position: relative;vertical-align: middle;\"><span style=\"text-align:center;display: block; padding: 0;\">1</span><span style=\"display: block; padding: 0;position: absolute; top: 0em; display: none;letter-spacing: -0.1em;\">_________</span><span style=\"display: block; padding: 0;border-top: thin solid black; text-align:center\">42</span></div>&nbsp;:&nbsp;<div style=\"display: inline-block;position: relative;vertical-align: middle;\"><span style=\"text-align:center;display: block; padding: 0;\">1</span><span style=\"display: block; padding: 0;position: absolute; top: 0em; display: none;letter-spacing: -0.1em;\">_________</span><span style=\"display: block; padding: 0;border-top: thin solid black; text-align:center\">35</span></div>&nbsp;and the month of Feb, respective ratio of their incomes becomes 1: 1: 1 while the sum of their monthly incomes remains same. If A receives Rs.5000 more in Jan than in Feb, then find the total income of C in Jan and Feb together.&nbsp;</div></p><p></p>", "q_hi": "<p><div>&#2332;&#2344;&#2357;&#2352;&#2368; &#2350;&#2361;&#2368;&#2344;&#2375; &#2350;&#2375;&#2306; &#2340;&#2368;&#2344; &#2357;&#2381;&#2351;&#2325;&#2381;&#2340;&#2367;&#2351;&#2379;&#2306; A, B &#2324;&#2352; C &#2325;&#2368; &#2310;&#2351; &#2325;&#2366; &#2360;&#2306;&#2348;&#2306;&#2343;&#2367;&#2340; &#2309;&#2344;&#2369;&#2346;&#2366;&#2340; <div style=\"display: inline-block;position: relative;vertical-align: middle;\"><span style=\"text-align:center;display: block; padding: 0;\">1</span><span style=\"display: block; padding: 0;position: absolute; top: 0em; display: none;letter-spacing: -0.1em;\">_________</span><span style=\"display: block; padding: 0;border-top: thin solid black; text-align:center\">30</span></div>&nbsp;:&nbsp;<div style=\"display: inline-block;position: relative;vertical-align: middle;\"><span style=\"text-align:center;display: block; padding: 0;\">1</span><span style=\"display: block; padding: 0;position: absolute; top: 0em; display: none;letter-spacing: -0.1em;\">_________</span><span style=\"display: block; padding: 0;border-top: thin solid black; text-align:center\">42</span></div>&nbsp;:&nbsp;<div style=\"display: inline-block;position: relative;vertical-align: middle;\"><span style=\"text-align:center;display: block; padding: 0;\">1</span><span style=\"display: block; padding: 0;position: absolute; top: 0em; display: none;letter-spacing: -0.1em;\">_________</span><span style=\"display: block; padding: 0;border-top: thin solid black; text-align:center\">35</span></div> &#2361;&#2376; &#2340;&#2341;&#2366; &#2347;&#2352;&#2357;&#2352;&#2368; &#2350;&#2361;&#2368;&#2344;&#2375; &#2350;&#2375;&#2306; &#2313;&#2344;&#2325;&#2368; &#2310;&#2351; &#2325;&#2366; &#2309;&#2344;&#2369;&#2346;&#2366;&#2340; 1 : 1 : 1 &#2361;&#2379; &#2332;&#2366;&#2340;&#2366; &#2361;&#2376; &#2332;&#2348;&#2325;&#2367; &#2313;&#2344;&#2325;&#2368; &#2350;&#2366;&#2360;&#2367;&#2325; &#2310;&#2351; &#2325;&#2366; &#2351;&#2379;&#2327; &#2360;&#2350;&#2366;&#2344; &#2352;&#2361;&#2340;&#2366; &#2361;&#2376;&#2404; &#2351;&#2342;&#2367; A &#2325;&#2379; &#2347;&#2352;&#2357;&#2352;&#2368; &#2325;&#2368; &#2340;&#2369;&#2354;&#2344;&#2366; &#2350;&#2375;&#2306; &#2332;&#2344;&#2357;&#2352;&#2368; &#2350;&#2361;&#2368;&#2344;&#2375; &#2350;&#2375;&#2306; 5000 &#2352;&#2369;&#2346;&#2351;&#2375; &#2309;&#2343;&#2367;&#2325; &#2346;&#2381;&#2352;&#2366;&#2346;&#2381;&#2340; &#2361;&#2379;&#2340;&#2375; &#2361;&#2376;&#2306;, &#2340;&#2379; &#2319;&#2325; &#2360;&#2366;&#2341; &#2332;&#2344;&#2357;&#2352;&#2368; &#2324;&#2352; &#2347;&#2352;&#2357;&#2352;&#2368; &#2350;&#2361;&#2368;&#2344;&#2375; &#2350;&#2375;&#2306; C &#2325;&#2368; &#2325;&#2369;&#2354; &#2310;&#2351; &#2332;&#2381;&#2334;&#2366;&#2340; &#2325;&#2368;&#2332;&#2367;&#2319;&#2404;</div></p>", "options_en": ["Rs.45000", "Rs.30000", "Rs.60000", "Rs.72000"], "options_hi": ["45000 &#2352;&#2369;&#2346;&#2351;&#2375;", "30000 &#2352;&#2369;&#2346;&#2351;&#2375;", "60000 &#2352;&#2369;&#2346;&#2351;&#2375;", "72000 &#2352;&#2369;&#2346;&#2351;&#2375;"], "answer": 2, "solution_en": "<p>Respective ratio of incomes of A, B and C in Jan = <img width=276 height=37 src=\"https://u1.oliveboard.in/exams/solution/oliveimg/p12450/image002.gif\"></p><p>Let incomes of A, B and C in Jan be '7x', '5x' and '6x' respectively.</p><p>Respective ratio of incomes of A, B and C in Feb = 1: 1: 1</p><p>Let incomes of A, B and C in Feb be 'y', 'y' and 'y' respectively.</p><p>According to the question:</p><p>7x + 5x + 6x = y + y + y</p><p>18x = 3y</p><p>y = 6x</p><p>And,</p><p>7x  -  y = 5000</p><p>7x  -  6x = 5000</p><p>x = 5000</p><p>Total income of C in Jan and Feb together = 6x + y</p><p>= 6x + 6x</p><p>= 12x</p><p>= 12 * 5000</p><p>= Rs.60000</p>", "solution_hi": "<p>Respective ratio of incomes of A, B and C in Jan = <img width=276 height=37 src=\"https://u1.oliveboard.in/exams/solution/oliveimg/p12450/image002.gif\"></p><p>Let incomes of A, B and C in Jan be '7x', '5x' and '6x' respectively.</p><p>Respective ratio of incomes of A, B and C in Feb = 1: 1: 1</p><p>Let incomes of A, B and C in Feb be 'y', 'y' and 'y' respectively.</p><p>According to the question:</p><p>7x + 5x + 6x = y + y + y</p><p>18x = 3y</p><p>y = 6x</p><p>And,</p><p>7x  -  y = 5000</p><p>7x  -  6x = 5000</p><p>x = 5000</p><p>Total income of C in Jan and Feb together = 6x + y</p><p>= 6x + 6x</p><p>= 12x</p><p>= 12 * 5000</p><p>= Rs.60000</p>"}, {"q_en": "<p>On a bookshelf, 48% of the number of English books is equal to two-third of the number of Hindi books. What is the ratio of the number of English books to that of Hindi on the shelf?</p>", "q_hi": "<p>&#2319;&#2325; &#2310;&#2354;&#2350;&#2366;&#2352;&#2368; (&#2348;&#2369;&#2325;&#2358;&#2375;&#2354;&#2381;&#2347;&#2364;) &#2350;&#2375;&#2306;, &#2309;&#2306;&#2327;&#2381;&#2352;&#2375;&#2332;&#2368; &#2325;&#2368; &#2346;&#2369;&#2360;&#2381;&#2340;&#2325;&#2379;&#2306; &#2325;&#2368; &#2360;&#2306;&#2326;&#2381;&#2351;&#2366; &#2325;&#2366; 48%, &#2361;&#2367;&#2306;&#2342;&#2368; &#2325;&#2368; &#2346;&#2369;&#2360;&#2381;&#2340;&#2325;&#2379;&#2306; &#2325;&#2368; &#2360;&#2306;&#2326;&#2381;&#2351;&#2366; &#2325;&#2375; 2/3 &#2349;&#2366;&#2327; &#2325;&#2375; &#2348;&#2352;&#2366;&#2348;&#2352; &#2361;&#2376;&#2404; &#2310;&#2354;&#2350;&#2366;&#2352;&#2368; &#2350;&#2375;&#2306; &#2309;&#2306;&#2327;&#2381;&#2352;&#2375;&#2332;&#2368; &#2325;&#2368; &#2346;&#2369;&#2360;&#2381;&#2340;&#2325;&#2379;&#2306; &#2325;&#2368; &#2360;&#2306;&#2326;&#2381;&#2351;&#2366; &#2324;&#2352; &#2361;&#2367;&#2306;&#2342;&#2368; &#2325;&#2368; &#2346;&#2369;&#2360;&#2381;&#2340;&#2325;&#2379;&#2306; &#2325;&#2368; &#2360;&#2306;&#2326;&#2381;&#2351;&#2366; &#2325;&#2366; &#2309;&#2344;&#2369;&#2346;&#2366;&#2340; &#2325;&#2367;&#2340;&#2344;&#2366; &#2361;&#2376;?</p>", "options_en": ["25: 12", "12: 25", "18: 25", "25: 18"], "options_hi": ["25: 12", "12: 25", "18: 25", "25: 18"], "answer": 3, "solution_en": "<p>Given that,</p><p>(48/100) * E = (2/3) * H</p><p>(12/25) * E = (2/3) * H</p><p>(18/25) * E = H</p><p>E/H = 25/18 = 25: 18</p>", "solution_hi": "<p>Given that,</p><p>(48/100) * E = (2/3) * H</p><p>(12/25) * E = (2/3) * H</p><p>(18/25) * E = H</p><p>E/H = 25/18 = 25: 18</p>"}, {"q_en": "<p>Two number are in the ratio 3: 5. If 9 is subtracted from each, the new numbers are in the ratio 12: 23. The smaller number is</p>", "q_hi": "<p>&#2342;&#2379; &#2360;&#2306;&#2326;&#2381;&#2351;&#2366;&#2323;&#2306; &#2325;&#2366; &#2309;&#2344;&#2369;&#2346;&#2366;&#2340; 3: 5 &#2361;&#2376;| &#2351;&#2342;&#2367; &#2346;&#2381;&#2352;&#2340;&#2381;&#2351;&#2375;&#2325; &#2350;&#2375;&#2306; &#2360;&#2375; 9 &#2328;&#2335;&#2366; &#2342;&#2367;&#2351;&#2366; &#2332;&#2366;&#2340;&#2366; &#2361;&#2376;, &#2340;&#2379; &#2344;&#2312; &#2360;&#2306;&#2326;&#2381;&#2351;&#2366;&#2323;&#2306; &#2325;&#2366; &#2309;&#2344;&#2369;&#2346;&#2366;&#2340; 12: 23 &#2361;&#2379; &#2332;&#2366;&#2340;&#2366; &#2361;&#2376;| &#2360;&#2348;&#2360;&#2375; &#2331;&#2379;&#2335;&#2368; &#2360;&#2306;&#2326;&#2381;&#2351;&#2366; &#2361;&#2376;-</p>", "options_en": ["27", "36", "45", "33"], "options_hi": ["27", "36", "45", "33"], "answer": 3, "solution_en": "<p>Let the numbers be 3n and 5n respectively.</p> <p>New numbers are 3n-9 and 5n-9 respectively.</p> <p>Given, (3n-9):(5n-9) = 12:23</p> <p>=&gt; 69n  -  207 = 60n  -  108</p> <p>=&gt; 9n = 99</p> <p>=&gt; n = 11</p> <p>Hence the numbers are 33 and 55</p>", "solution_hi": "<p>Let the numbers be 3n and 5n respectively.</p> <p>New numbers are 3n-9 and 5n-9 respectively.</p> <p>Given, (3n-9):(5n-9) = 12:23</p> <p>=&gt; 69n  -  207 = 60n  -  108</p> <p>=&gt; 9n = 99</p> <p>=&gt; n = 11</p> <p>Hence the numbers are 33 and 55</p>"}]}